# Project Conventions

## File Naming

- React components: `kebab-case.tsx` (e.g., `agent-selector.tsx`, `chat-wrapper.tsx`)
- Utilities: `kebab-case.ts` (e.g., `runtime-switch.ts`)
- API routes: Next.js App Router convention (`route.ts` in directory)

## Imports

- Use `@/*` alias for all `src/` imports.
- Group imports: 1) external packages, 2) `@/` internal, 3) relative.
- No barrel exports (`index.ts`) unless the directory has 5+ public exports.

## TypeScript

- Strict mode. No `any` without an eslint-disable comment and justification.
- Prefer `type` over `interface` unless extending is needed.
- Export types alongside their usage, not in separate type files.

## React

- Functional components only.
- Prefer named exports over default exports.
- Mark client components with `"use client"` only when necessary.
- Server components are the default in App Router.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS only. No CSS modules, no styled-components.
- Custom CSS only in `globals.css` for CSS custom properties and overrides.
- Use `cn()` utility (from `@/lib/utils`) for conditional class merging.

## Testing

- Tests live next to their source: `foo.test.ts` beside `foo.ts`.
- Use Vitest for unit tests.
- Use Playwright for E2E tests (when added).

## Git

- Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`.
- One concern per commit.
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, or secrets.
